- Is that hard?

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:07.757
- Well, you know what,

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:08.679
I'm not gonna say it's loose

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:10.592
because I'm the one that did
all the (beep) that was wrong.

00:00:10.592 --> 00:00:11.604
It's not loosely based.

00:00:11.604 --> 00:00:12.437
- (indistinct)

00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:13.270
- Is like, I know,

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.400
but I'm just saying, is that hard?

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.810
Like, to like, I don't know

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:16.950
like, it's hard for me sometimes

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.110
I write a lot about my
real life in songs, right?

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.301
It's hard for me to like rehash that.

00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:22.134
Is that hard?

00:00:22.134 --> 00:00:22.967
- Yeah, I would have
to say there are times

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:24.060
times where it is challenging,

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.673
but we're, I like to think, is that

00:00:25.673 --> 00:00:28.230
this is such an opportunity to heal

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.872
and I've always wanted my
pain to mean something.

00:00:30.872 --> 00:00:32.538
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- You know, as you've done

00:00:32.538 --> 00:00:35.430
like, to reach out and
carry much as people

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.050
and know that healing isn't linear,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.303
that you're not perfect and

00:00:38.303 --> 00:00:39.136
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:39.136 --> 00:00:41.100
- You know, just having empathy
you know, as you get older

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.780
